> I haven't been able to ascend a weaponless, atheist, polyless and vegan
> monk. Heck I haven't been able to ascend any monk.

I agree with the poster upthread that you shouldn't try to do all
those conducts right off. My first monk ascension was weaponless and
vegetarian (not vegan), my second was vegan/weaponless/polyless/
artwishless. Atheist I've only attempted with a priestess so far.

> Right now the ideal kit for an ascension bound monk, IMHO, would be
> gauntlets of power, speed boots, EOW, reflection and a ring.

GoP hinder spellcasting a lot unless you have a robe. With a robe you
give up wearing a CoMR, and your MR-granting quest artifact can be
stolen. Royal jelly can help get your strength up if you're willing to
be vegetarian rather than vegan. Reflection is a must for any
character IMHO. As monks shouldn't wear body armor, that will occupy
your amulet slot (so no life saving).

> What I can't between a ring of increase damage or increase accuracy. Of
> course I'd enchant these up to their max.

I'd save ring slots for slow digestion/free action/conflict (the last
only when necessary).

